      "correct": true,
      "connector_calls": 2,
      "answer": "python/rgp_bootstrap.py bootstrap validates ZIP members, rejects separators/traversal and symlinks, checks limits and hashes, then reads bytes rather than extracting paths. Replacing this with unrestricted extractall() could overwrite files outside the intended output directory or trust attacker-supplied paths. docs/RGP_SECURITY_MODEL.md explicitly treats all RGP/ZIP content as untrusted.",
